2. Make `Matrix` a struct `type Matrix struct { rows [][]int }` — but in that case, `matrix == nil` won't compile. The benchmark has `if matrix == nil` — a struct isn't comparable with nil. So this is a no-go.

Therefore, the interface approach is the correct one. The test file is calling methods through Matrix, so the interface needs to include Rows, Cols, and Set.

